<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korean Air, Sikorsky in helicopter deal.</title>
<headline>Korean Air, Sikorsky in helicopter deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korean Air Lines Co Ltd (KAL), said on Thursday it has agreed with U.S.-based Sikorsky Aircraft Corp to jointly invest $400 million over the next six years to develop multi-purpose helicopters.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to develop prototype helicopters by 2000. Full production will be possible by 2003,&quot; said Kim Sung-joon, a KAL spokesman.</p>
<p>He said further details of the joint venture were not available. Sikorsky Aircraft Corp is a unit of United Technologies Corp.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
